# Design Logs

When proposing a design (architecture, dataflow, UI structure, module boundaries, or similar), save a markdown snapshot under the project-root `.design-logs/` directory (flat — files directly under that folder, not nested).

## When to write

- After drafting a design proposal in chat (or before asking the user to choose among options).
- Not required for trivial one-line suggestions or pure implementation follow-ups with no new design.

## File naming

```
YYYY-MM-DD-HHmm-<short-kebab-topic>.md
```

Example: `2026-08-06-2357-layout-editor-store.md`

## Snapshot contents

- Title and date
- Problem / goal
- Proposed approach (and alternatives if discussed)
- Key decisions or open questions
- Keep it self-contained so later sessions can recover the proposal without the chat

## Notes

- Append-only: do not overwrite or delete earlier snapshots unless the user asks.
- English or Japanese is fine; match the proposal language used in chat.
